---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About Ali Parchekani — PhD candidate, educator, and applied ML engineer at the University of Toronto."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="About" title="Ali Parchekani" />

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="space-y-7 text-[16.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted">

      <p class="font-serif text-xl md:text-[22px] leading-relaxed text-ink" data-reveal>
        I am a PhD candidate in Electrical and Computer Engineering at the University of Toronto,
        working in the Wireless Internet Research Lab under Professor Shahrokh Valaee. My doctoral
        research centers on intelligent wireless sensing — specifically, how Reconfigurable Intelligent
        Surfaces (RIS) can be optimized to enable precise radar-based localization and sensing in complex
        environments. My work combines optimization theory (evolutionary algorithms, Markov Chain Monte
        Carlo, convex relaxation) with model-based deep learning, and has resulted in four peer-reviewed
        IEEE conference publications with manuscripts currently under review.
      </p>

      <p data-reveal>
        Before Toronto, I completed my M.Sc. in Electrical Engineering — Communication Systems at
        the University of Tehran, graduating <strong class="text-ink">ranked 1st</strong> in my cohort, and my B.Sc.
        in the same department, finishing <strong class="text-ink">ranked 3rd</strong>. My M.Sc. has been
        credential-evaluated as equivalent to a U.S. M.S. in Electrical Engineering
        (Communication Systems emphasis). I expect to complete my PhD in <strong class="text-ink">August 2026</strong>.
      </p>

      <p data-reveal>
        Alongside my research, teaching has always been central to how I work. I have supported
        instruction across <strong class="text-ink">40+ distinct University of Toronto courses</strong> — spanning
        UTM, UTSC, and St. George — as a teaching assistant and course instructor. The courses range
        from introductory programming and calculus to machine learning, AI, data structures, and
        communication networks. I have also independently designed and taught pre-university enrichment
        courses for high school students: a games, strategy, and AI course in which students built
        playable AI-enabled prototypes, and two iterations of a critical thinking in statistics course.
        Student evaluations consistently highlight clear explanation, patience, and the ability to make
        abstract ideas concrete.
      </p>

      <p data-reveal>
        On the industry side, I have spent six-plus years building ML systems in production and research
        settings. At HARA AI in Tehran, I developed the NLU layer for a Persian automated call-center,
        working with transformer models on a 10M+ sentence corpus. At the University of Tehran, I built
        ML pipelines for network traffic classification using deep learning. My current research involves
        end-to-end simulation pipelines, config-driven experiment management, and the kind of rigorous
        experimental design that bridges academic rigor with engineering practice. More recently I have
        been building agentic AI systems — multi-agent architectures with LangGraph, OpenAI Agents SDK,
        and CrewAI — and exploring the intersection of language models and autonomous task completion.
      </p>

      <p class="border-l-2 border-blue-700 pl-5 text-ink" data-reveal>
        I am based in Toronto, Ontario, and available for academic teaching positions, high-touch STEM
        tutoring (in-person in the GTA or online), and engineering/research collaborations.
      </p>

      <div class="pt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-4" data-reveal>
        <a
          href={`${BASE}/teaching/`}
          class="inline-block bg-blue-700 text-on-accent font-semibold px-5 py-3 hover:bg-blue-500 transition-colors text-sm"
        >
          Teaching profile
        </a>
        <a
          href={`${BASE}/research/`}
          class="inline-block border border-blue-700 text-blue-700 font-semibold px-5 py-3 hover:bg-blue-700 hover:text-on-accent transition-colors text-sm"
        >
          Research
        </a>
        <a
          href={`${BASE}/contact/`}
          class="inline-block border border-line text-muted font-semibold px-5 py-3 hover:border-blue-700 hover:text-blue-700 transition-colors text-sm"
        >
          Get in touch
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
